    "title": "Wheeling Park alum and star of viral TikTok video returns to host show about being yourself - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Wheeling, W.Va. (WTRF) – One local thespian and TikTok star is returning to the Ohio Valley to put on a show about the merits of being yourself. Megan Chacalos is a Wheeling Park High School theatre alum, and has been working in the theatre scene in New York City. Late last year, her story about a high school mishap involving olive oil went viral on TikTok, racking up tens of millions of views. This weekend, Megan, as well as her partner, Jake Bryan Guthrie, will be putting on a show at Oglebay Institute’s Towngate Theatre, all about how she found success by being herself. “It’s half standup, half show tunes. So you’ll hear songs from theater legends like Liza Minnelli, Judy Garland, Barbra Streisand, but then also just me yapping like I like to do in a comical style. It’s fun for the whole family, there’s going to be a lot of laughs, a lot of me oversharing.” The shows will take place at the Towngate Theater this Friday and Saturday at 7:00pm. All proceeds will go to the Open Door Kitchen at St. John The Divine Greek Orthodox Church, and flood victim relief organized by Ohio County Schools teachers. CLICK HERE TO BUY TICKETS For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WTRF.",
